# This repo is the STUDENT-FACING subset of the course only.
# Everything below stays out of git on purpose - instructor answer keys,
# solved notebooks, and the build source (which embeds correct answers
# directly in the assessment source files) never belong where students
# can reach them.

# Instructor-only deliverables
02-notebooks/instructor/
03-exercises/Answer-Keys.*
04-assessment/answer-key.md

# Build source and tooling - not something students need, and several of
# these files embed the pre/post-test answer key directly (isCorrect
# flags, ANSWER_KEY dict) or the mini-project's Hansen-loss reference value.
build/
04-assessment/questions.py
04-assessment/baseline_questions.py
04-assessment/make_forms.gs
04-assessment/make_baseline_form.gs
04-assessment/gain_score.ipynb

# HTML sources - students receive the rendered PDFs, not the source.
01-slides/*.html
01-slides/theme/
00-setup/*.html
05-handouts/*.html
03-exercises/Exercise-Day*.html
03-exercises/*-fillable.html
04-assessment/*.html

# Compiled Python bytecode. IMPORTANT: this is not just clutter - importing
# questions.py or baseline_questions.py (e.g. via make_assessment.py) makes
# Python cache a compiled .pyc of that exact module, which is trivially
# decompiled back to source. The answer key must never end up here either.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Instructor documentation about how this whole package was built/verified.
README.md

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
